THE SALT ROAD}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch
by Henry Aldous}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\pagebb\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Chapter One}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
The Caravan}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The caravan left the city before dawn, forty camels and nine men, and by the time the sun was up the walls were only a brown line on the horizon behind them.}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Idris rode at the rear, where the dust was worst, because he was the youngest and because nobody had told him he could ride anywhere else.}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
On the third night they camped at the dry well. The old drivers called it }{\loch\i\loch
the Liar}{\loch
, because it had promised water to three generations of travellers and given none.}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
"Do not drink from it even if it fills," said Rahim. "Especially if it fills."}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch
#}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
In the morning the well was full to the brim.}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\pagebb\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Chapter Two}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\qc\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
The Liar}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Nobody spoke of it at breakfast. The men loaded the camels with their backs to the water, and Rahim counted the animals twice, which he had never done before.}
\par \pard\plain \s16\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
Idris counted too. There were forty-one.}
\par }